WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.160
Nicole: All organisations and
companies will have an IT policy

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.520
in place, and some may even have
a specific cyber security policy.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.879
All policies should be adhered to
consistently from the top down.

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:16.989
They should be clear and current
being reviewed and updated by the

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:21.070
senior management team at least
annually, and in touch with ever

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.840
changing laws and regulations.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.619
There should be no barriers to
complying with policy guidelines

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:30.220
and procedures and where necessary
training should be provided.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.719
There should also be regular audits
to check that policy is being followed

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.929
and all employees are on track.

00:00:38.029 --> 00:00:41.440
Most new employees must sign up to
a policy agreement as part of their

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.420
induction to say that they will follow
the guidelines before they are given

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.420
their emails and log in details.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:52.159
Policy guidelines may be different
depending on the business or organisation

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:56.500
and the data that employees are working
with but overall, the guidelines

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.989
will be the same for everyone.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.160
Where any specific sensitive
data is concerned there may be

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.090
extra level of security involved
and different rules may apply.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.369
Where data is concerned guidelines
should be always followed

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.800
strictly adhering to GDPR rules.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.330
There are a range of ethical rules that
link to legislation when it comes to

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.930
using computer systems that apply such as:

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.260
Not using computer
equipment to harm others.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.640
Not interfering with
other’s computers and work

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.939
Not looking through other’s
files without their permission.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.039
Not using a computer to
steal or cause mischief.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.510
Not copying software.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.660
Not using other people’s
resources without permission.

00:01:39.139 --> 00:01:41.220
Acting without regard for consequences.

00:01:41.509 --> 00:01:43.990
And having respect for data security.

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:48.339
With remote working, many more
employees are working from home

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.640
and these rules should still apply.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.530
Many employees now sync their work
emails to their smartphones, which may

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.710
involve employers expecting workers
to check emails outside office hours.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.900
Cyber security is even more important
especially when personal emails are

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.130
accessed alongside business emails.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:12.369
Many businesses will set up their
employees for remote working but in

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:17.129
some cases, it may involve an employee
taking their laptop home and relying

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.140
on their own internet security set up.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:24.810
All IT policy guidelines regarding
data security and misuse of computers

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.720
should be still adhered to even more so.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.549
Unethical conduct can be something as
simple as leaving a 'post it' around

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.600
with log details for anyone to access
a computer system as this can open a

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.200
system up to unethical security issues.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.850
This may just be thoughtless
behaviour or a lack of judgement,

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.109
but it can lead to so much more.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.819
It may involve deliberately copying
information and data to use or supply

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.840
to others for unethical activities.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.589
Unethical behaviour can involve
sabotage, disclosing or misusing

00:02:57.589 --> 00:03:02.320
confidential information or maliciously
injuring the reputation or prospects

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.020
of an individual or business.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.330
It’s also important to remember
that as cyber security professionals

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:12.609
we have a great deal of access to
sensitive data and it’s important

00:03:12.639 --> 00:03:16.180
that we do not use this high level
of access for the wrong purposes.

